.TH "GCMallocChild" "3" "2026\-11\-06" "GCmalloc"
.SH NAME
\fBGCMallocChild\fR \- allocate memory and set dependencies
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function like \fBGCMalloc\fR(3), but not set pointer to roots, but set
pointer as dependency to \fIparent\fR
.SH RETURN VALUE
Return value is just allocated child\&.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
.RS 4
/* \&.\&.\&. */
User* parent = (User*)GCMalloc(sizeof(User));
User* child = (User*)GCMallocChild(sizeof(User), parent);
/* While living parent, child not be deleted, but if need that
   parent not deletes when child is living, uncomment this: */
/* GCAddDependency(child, parent); */
/* \&.\&.\&. */
.fi
.RE
